<title>USA: Fed's Broaddus says price stability a stimulus.</title>
<headline>Fed's Broaddus says price stability a stimulus.</headline>
<dateline>WILMINGTON, Ind. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Richmond Federal Reserve president Alfred Broaddus said on Thursday that price stability, far from hindering growth, is an extraordinary stimulus to growth.</p>
<p>&quot;We need to make the case that price stability, far from hindering growth over any reasonable period of time, is an extraordinary stimulus to growth,&quot; said Broaddus, who was speaking to students and faculty at Indiana University.</p>
</text>
